+## Summary
+
+Implement one pure Python function in `src/reminders.py`. It will validate confirmed action mappings, parse only UTC ISO-8601 timestamps, derive the normal or five-minute fallback reminder time, and serialize output timestamps with `Z`.
+
+## Technical Approach
+
+Use Python's standard-library `datetime` module; no package or persistence layer is required. Normalize a trailing `Z` to `+00:00` for parsing and reject timestamps that have no UTC offset or whose offset is not zero. Treat `confirmed is True` as an identity check so values such as `1` do not schedule reminders. Serialize all output through one helper that emits a trailing `Z`, and construct a fresh dictionary without modifying `action`.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+- Requires: Python standard library only.
+- Provides: deterministic reminder payloads to downstream scheduling code.
+
+## Testing Strategy
+
+- Unit tests use `unittest` in `tests/test_reminders.py`.
+- Test the normal 24-hour path, five-minute fallback, all strict boundaries, validation failures, exact-`True` confirmation, UTC serialization, determinism, and input immutability.
+- No integration test applies: the function has no I/O boundary.
+
+## Technical Context
+
+**Language/Version**: Python 3 (standard library only)
+**Primary Dependencies**: `datetime`
+**Storage**: N/A
+**Testing**: `python3 -m unittest`
+**Target Platform**: Python runtime
+**Project Type**: single-module backend utility
+**Performance Goals**: constant work per invocation
+**Constraints**: UTC-only emitted timestamps; no input mutation
+
+## Constitution Check
+
+No project constitution or context artifact exists in this isolated corpus. The applicable local quality gates are explicit validation, deterministic output, boundary coverage, and a passing standard-library test run.
+
+## Project Structure
+
+```
+src/reminders.py                 # implementation
+tests/test_reminders.py          # unit tests
+specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/E002-reminders/stories/S006-build-reminder/
+├── spec.md
