+├── data-model.md
+├── quickstart.md
+└── tasks.md
+```
+
+## Research Informing This Plan
+
+No external research is needed: Python's `datetime.fromisoformat`, `timedelta`, and `timezone.utc` cover the specified behavior without a new dependency.
+
+## Planning Phase 1: Design & Contracts
+
+- `data-model.md` documents the action input and reminder output mappings.
+- There is no HTTP or third-party API contract; the Python function signature is the contract.
+- `quickstart.md` records executable boundary scenarios.
+
+## Planning Phase 2: Implementation Guidance
+
+| FR ID | Requirement | Acceptance criteria | Priority |
+|-------|-------------|---------------------|----------|
+| FR-001 | Ignore actions unless `confirmed is True` | AC-3 | Critical |
+| FR-002 | Validate confirmed action identity and UTC due time | AC-3 | Critical |
+| FR-003 | Schedule 24 hours before a future due time | AC-1 | Critical |
+| FR-004 | Use only a strictly-valid five-minute fallback | AC-2 | Critical |
+| FR-005 | Return deterministic, `Z`-serialized payload without mutation | AC-1, AC-3 | High |
+
+### Key implementation decisions
+
+1. Use exact boolean identity (`is True`) for confirmation; it is the literal contract.
+2. Parse a trailing `Z` as UTC and reject other offsets, naïve values, and non-strings.
+3. Compare using timezone-aware UTC `datetime` values. The fallback condition is `fallback < due_at`, not `<=`.
+4. Keep parsing and formatting in private helpers to make invalid input behavior consistent and testable.
